6. SKILL — Excel Comparison

Purpose

Compare two structurally similar Excel datasets and identify differences.

Required Inputs

* baseline file;
* working/current file;
* table name;
* unique key column;
* descriptive/name column where applicable;
* columns to monitor.

Comparison Rules

Use the supplied unique identifier as the primary key.

Never use employee/person name as the unique identifier unless the user explicitly confirms that it is genuinely unique.

Detect:

* changed values;
* new records;
* optionally deleted records;
* blanks versus populated values;
* zero versus blank;
* duplicate identifiers.

Output

Prefer structured JSON grouped by record.

Example:

{
“employeeId”: “100236”,
“employeeName”: “Faraz Khan”,
“changes”: [
{
“field”: “Bonus Amount”,
“oldValue”: 3000,
“newValue”: 4000
},
{
“field”: “Salary”,
“oldValue”: 65000,
“newValue”: 68000
}
]
}

Prefer grouping changes before Power Automate when doing so substantially simplifies the flow.

