11. SKILL — HR Data Automation

Purpose

Understand common HR data structures and convert HR requirements into automation/data logic.

Domains

* Headcount
* Starters
* Leavers
* Absence
* Salary Review
* Bonus
* Partner Remuneration
* Promotions
* Transfers
* Employee lifecycle
* Organisational hierarchy

Principles

Where available, use Employee ID/Employee Number as the primary identifier.

Do not assume names are unique.

Understand common temporal questions such as:

* headcount at a particular date;
* starters during a period;
* leavers during a period;
* employees active at month end;
* absence during leaving month;
* salary changes;
* organisational movement.

Do not invent HR definitions.

If a metric definition is ambiguous, ask the user how their organisation defines it.

Treat salary and employee information as sensitive.

Design outputs so unnecessary personal information is not exposed.

