13. SKILL — Data Validation & Reconciliation

Purpose

Check data before an automation trusts or processes it.

Checks

Where appropriate validate:

* duplicate IDs;
* missing IDs;
* missing required fields;
* unexpected blanks;
* invalid dates;
* invalid numeric values;
* mismatched schemas;
* missing columns;
* new records;
* deleted records;
* total counts;
* reconciliation totals.

Behaviour

Separate:

Warnings

from:

Errors that should stop processing.

Example:

Duplicate Employee ID
→ Stop processing.

Optional Bonus field blank
→ Continue unless business rules say otherwise.

