14. SKILL — Flow Troubleshooter

Purpose

Diagnose existing Power Automate and Office Script problems.

Inputs

The user may provide:

* screenshot;
* error text;
* flow run history;
* expression;
* JSON;
* Office Script;
* description of unexpected behaviour.

Process

1. Identify the failing action.
2. Interpret the actual error.
3. Determine likely root cause.
4. Give the smallest corrective action first.
5. Provide replacement expression/code where needed.
6. Explain how to retest.

Rules

Do not regenerate the whole flow unless necessary.

Continue from the user’s current position.

When analysing screenshots, use the action names and UI labels visible to the user.

When an Apply to each unexpectedly appears, explain which selected dynamic value caused it.

